<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    docs/plan/03 § src — "connections, command builder, informers, SSA (09)".

    ⚠ THIS IS THE BOUNDARY ASSEMBLY OF docs/plan/03 § Assembly graph rules, RULE 3: "No assembly
    above CyberCloud.Kubernetes references k8s.Models." This is the assembly that may, and it is the
    only one in the platform that does. Everything it exposes upwards is expressed in
    CyberCloud.Kubernetes.Contracts' JSON-and-GUID vocabulary, so that a provider reconciler — which
    is above this — never names a Kubernetes type.

    ⚠ KubernetesClient 19.0.2, and the one thing that actually changed from Survival's 18.0.13.
    docs/plan/02 § Data, transport, Kubernetes asserts "19 changed the generic client surface — a
    small migration, done once, here" without naming it. Verified by diffing the public surface of
    both assemblies (18.0.13 vs 19.0.2, net10.0): the ONLY change to the generic-object surface is

      -  Task<T> GenericClient.ListAsync<T>(CancellationToken cancel = default)
      +  Task<T> GenericClient.ListAsync<T>(string labelSelector = null, string fieldSelector = null,
      +      int? limit = null, string continueToken = null, CancellationToken cancel = default)

    (and the same for ListNamespacedAsync). ICustomObjectsOperations — the interface server-side
    apply actually goes through — is byte-identical between the two versions. The migration cost is
    therefore exactly: a call written as `ListAsync<T>(ct)` no longer compiles and becomes
    `ListAsync<T>(cancel: ct)`. Everything else in the 18→19 diff is generated-model churn tracking
    Kubernetes 1.34 → 1.35 (alpha→beta graduations of StorageVersionMigration and
    PodCertificateRequest, removal of storage.k8s.io/v1alpha1 VolumeAttributesClass).

    The change is a gain rather than a cost for this assembly: in 18.0.13 GenericClient could not
    list by label selector at all, and docs/plan/09 § Observing filters every informer by
    `cybercloud.io/managed-by=cybercloud`.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The boundary. Nothing above this assembly may reference it — rule 3. -->
    <PackageReference Include="KubernetesClient" />
    <!-- Grain implementations, reminders, IIncomingGrainCallFilter. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Orleans.Server" />
    <!-- GrainId.GetTenantId(), for the caller-tenant check the null-tenant key cannot make. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Orleans.Multitenant" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.Core/CyberCloud.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.Core.Contracts/CyberCloud.Core.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.Kubernetes.Contracts/CyberCloud.Kubernetes.Contracts.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
